  "body": "The promise returned by BaseReadableStream.wait() which is [[readablePromise]] is rejected with TypeError when it reaches EOF. So, wait() seems to be basically only for waiting for the \"readable\" state. Someone could imagine from the very generic name \"wait()\" that it'll wait for any change of state happen on the object. So, I suggest that we document well that wait() is rejected on EOF or do some renaming or change its semantics for something better (I don't know for now).\n\nAlso, in the \"Using read()/wait()/state\" example, readableStream is watched by using wait() but EOF hits it by TypeError and will be handled by \"e => console.error(e)\" where I believe we should print \"--- all done!\" as well as the case right above it. We need fix on it?\n",
